{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules","id":1300092,"title":"Various Mage Houserules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-26T14:30:23-07:00","id":1300092,"title":"Various Mage Houserules","content":"- Affinity Sphere is tied to Arete rating. So if you buy Arete 3, you have to set up your Sphere dot spread so that you have 3 dots in your Affinity Sphere. When you do a successful seeking you pay the normal cost for Arete increase, and your Affinity Sphere rises to meet your Arete rating.<br /> <br /> I like this because from a story-telling/cinematic perspective, there is something so awesome about a person gaining new powers when they have that epiphany. Your Arete increases to 2, your Life goes up to 2, you find you can heal yourself, that sort of thing. It also means players feel a really strong connection to the Affinity Sphere since it becomes part of those special moments.<br /> <br /> - EXP gets split into Mundane/Arcane EXP. Mundane buys Abilities, Attributes, Willpower, Mental/Physical/Social Merits, backgrounds that Sleepers can have. Arcane buys Arete, Spheres, Supernatural Merits, and backgrounds like Totem and Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The beauty of this is balanced growth is ensured. If you give 2 M and 1 A each session, for example, people develop the Abilities of their mage's practice over time, investing in the WAY their mage does magick, not just in dots in Spheres. People feel empowered to invest large amounts of EXP into things like Etiquette, Expression, High Ritual, Finance and Politics, because they know that they're not &quot;falling behind&quot; in terms of raw magickal power. They know that everyone's got the exact same amount of EXP to put into spheres/arete, so they don't have to sweat the details or worry about the risks of not min-maxing in a competitive game with opposing PCs, for example. I'm seeing the PCs just... flourish, basically, under this system, with loving care going into little details like how they train their abilities and what they plan to do in the future, and even people spending points on frivolous things that don't feed into their magick directly. Plus Attributes and Willpower are so expensive in terms of EXP that I can't imagine PCs investing much in them otherwise, when they can get so much more bang for their buck with magickal stuff.<br /> <br /> Essentially the reason I love this change is that it makes sure that magick is more than what spheres you have, and what arete you've reached. It helps direct the attention of the PCs towards how their abilities feed into their magick, and ensures that the abilities that form their practice get some love. And on top of all of that it means you can give loads of EXP without being scared of the repercussions, and without having to carefully curate what your PCs purchase. Mundane EXP is safe (short of ludicrous amounts), Arcane EXP is potentially dangerous if you give too much, so you can keep that in mind when balancing what you give.<br /> <br /> - EDIT: Neglected to mention a big houserule. I give the same EXP to all players at the end of a session, and I include players who aren't present. It just ensures that all PCs advance at roughly the same rate, and doesn't punish people for being busy IRL. And if you're having a bad day and struggle to RP well it doesn't mean you'll miss out on EXP. It's just simpler, never been a fan of WoD's 'earned' experience system, although the guidelines might be useful for deciding how much EXP to give the group as a whole. So if it's been a big important session I'll just say &quot;everyone add 4 mundane and 1 arcane to their sheet&quot;.<br /> <br /> - Totem is broadened up somewhat; Shamans are still the masters of it, but you can have a Saint as your &quot;totem&quot; if you like, or one of the gods in your pantheon, or one of your ancestors. It doesn't have to be Tiger or Spider or similar. It just suggests a bond with a spirit, and the nature of that bond varies, as long as you aren't in charge of them (if you want to be in charge, get a spirit familiar).<br /> <br /> - I like the Data Sphere, but the connections table is a total mess. Several hours for each roll? That is just the opposite of fun. I simply rewrote the normal Correspondence connections table to have Data-style connections instead of the standard connections. Essentially at my table Data has a few downsides and requirements (computers need to be a major part of your practice, work is a bit slower and more deliberate, it's much harder to justify working without tools, you can't form a connection with anything that has no connection to the world of digitized information (from antediluvians to hermit mages in the andes)), and a few cool upsides (typically coincidental because technology is winning out in most reality zones, supported by a huge global connected network, links to the digital web, allows interaction with computers more easily than correspondence, lets you work with connections that wouldn't work for correspondence, you can exploit information easily found online).<br /> * <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Successes needed</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Range; distance between operator and targeted place/system/object.</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Connection; what the operator has that connects them to the targeted place/system/object. More successes are needed if the connection is weak.</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Line of Sight, Shared Network</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body Sample, Source Code, Information on subject from database</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target is Very Familiar</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Close possession or companion, sample code, personal email or social media account</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target is Familiar</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Possession or casual friend, legacy code, sockpuppet, throwaway email or social media account</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target was Visited Once</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Casual acquaintance or object used once, derivative code, IP address</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Described Location or System</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Briefly met or touched object or person, code from same language, rerouted IP string</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6+</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anywhere on Earth or Digital Web</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No Connection</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> *<br /> - Anyone with a hypereconomic practice can take Primal Utility, it is not the personal property of the Syndicate. The VAs have more people who are into cryptocurrency and digital economy as well.<br /> <br /> - Just pretend that the Blood Treachery rules on Ghouldom, and the optional Avatar/Arete-melting rules in M20, don't exist. I can see what they were going for but Ghoul is a 6 point *merit*, not a 6 point *flaw*. It is also a merit with a lot of downsides already tacked onto it. It doesn't need a metaphysical destruction of the mage's control of reality that slowly happens over time. A smarter story about addiction will use actual IRL negative consequences of addiction rather than making up supernatural ones. The latter is easy, but cheap. What makes this even more silly is that all of these rules were invented to stop Ghouldom from being too powerful. &quot;What if they put points into Thaumaturgy, then we'll be really screwed!!!&quot;. I just... I can't see what they were going for there. There's nothing threatening about a Mage who spends 20 EXP (or whatever extortionate rate Ghouls have to pay) to use low level static magic. All EXP put into Fortitude is EXP you could be putting into Arete and Spheres. Besides, if you don't want them to have Celerity... just... tell them they can't have Celerity. Issue solved. No need to say yes and then plot to steal their Avatar rating for daring to purchase a merit *you let them have in the first place*.<br /> <br /> The tl;dr would be that if you don't want a PC to take the Ghoul merit, don't let them take it. That's just way easier.<br /> <br /> - The Arcane Background is capped at 1 at character gen, and only granted if it suits the character. It's far too open to abuse in my opinion, and the opinion of one of my Mage ST friends. The mild effect of blending into the background and slipping out of the foreground in people's memories is quite cool. I also like the idea of someone just being naturally forgettable and sneaky kind of by giving off less of an &quot;I Am Here&quot; signal. But at 3+ it's just a case of existing in a world without consequences where you're sort of detached from RP simply by being so hard to notice. So it's simultaneously too bad and too good, and all at the cost of 5 freebie points for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-27-2019, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T00:31:08-07:00","id":1300211,"title":"","content":"I take the Primal Utility thing one step further: I allow other Practices than Hypereconomics to access it. In particular, my Choristers have access to a variation of it where instead of providing access to Primal Ventures that are exceptional examples of industry and innovation, it provides access to Primal Fellowships that are exceptional examples of compassion, prudence, and faith. The game systems are the same, except that investing time and effort to support the Fellowship is preferred over just throwing money their way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T01:07:12-07:00","id":1300214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300211#post1300211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take the Primal Utility thing one step further: I allow other Practices than Hypereconomics to access it. In particular, my Choristers have access to a variation of it where instead of providing access to Primal Ventures that are exceptional examples of industry and innovation, it provides access to Primal Fellowships that are exceptional examples of compassion, prudence, and faith. The game systems are the same, except that investing time and effort to support the Fellowship is preferred over just throwing money their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually such a cool idea. So I'm imagining that a Priest/Rabbi/etc with PU instead of Prime is going to harness the faith, compassion and belief of their religious community to fuel their magick. Essentially make it the same as the chart for accessing Primal Ventures, but remove the option of simply throwing money at it via investment, and add the caveat of the community needing to match your faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:29:02-07:00","id":1300241,"title":"","content":"I am also imagining that members of any government or non-profit agency or community group could potentially find use for Utility that they invest themselves in and incorporate into their paradigm. An NWO prospect in the IRS who recently awoke but hasn't shown the outward signs may well still develop some form of Utility based on their incorporation of agency procedures and beliefs, and their investment into the same, into their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:38:34-07:00","id":1300244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300214#post1300214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually such a cool idea. So I'm imagining that a Priest/Rabbi/etc with PU instead of Prime is going to harness the faith, compassion and belief of their religious community to fuel their magick. Essentially make it the same as the chart for accessing Primal Ventures, but remove the option of simply throwing money at it via investment, and add the caveat of the community needing to match your faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Though also, it's worth noting that the \u201cexample of industry and innovation\u201d bit was in the original write-up of Primal Utility in the <b>Revised Syndicate Convention Book</b>, but got lost in translation in <b>M20</b>; and I consider it to be a vital restriction on Primal Utility, as it keeps the Syndicate from tapping into every small business nationwide and instead causes them to focus on a select few ventures that have a special quality to them, as well as to focus on getting more personally involved in their Ventures in order to safeguard their investments. <br /> <br /> The Chorister equivalent of this is that you can't just harness any and all religious centers, as the vast majority of churches, synagogues, and mosques <i>aren't</i> the focal points of religious virtue that they claim to be: especially in the World of Darkness, far too many of them are spiritually dead or corrupt. With Primal Utility (which the Choristers would likely have a different name for, reflecting their view that it's not so much about Utility as it is about virtue), the mage would be well-equipped to identify those true fellowships that actually <i>do</i> exemplify the religious beliefs that the Celestial Chorus espouses (and this qualify for the equivalent of \u201cPrimal Venture\u201d status, which also needs a different name when views through the Chorister Focus), though his next task would be identifying just what it is about that particular congregation that makes it special and then doing everything he can to nurture and protect it. <br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I singled out the Celestial Chorus for this initially because traditionally they've held the Seat of Prime; but it also makes sense for their take on just what Prime <i>is</i> to be one that's rooted in human beliefs and activities as opposed to the \u201cmystical energies\u201d that a Hermetic make tends to think of when she contemplates Prime, albeit different beliefs and activities than the ones that the Syndicate favors. I'm reminded of an old <b><i>GURPS Religion</i></b> supplement that took the standard GURPS Magic system with its Mana Levels and Magic Items and achieved a more religious flavor through some simple relabeling: Mana became Sanctity, Magery was replaced by Power Investiture, and Magic Items became Holy Items. Shifting the Celestial Chorus from Prime to \u201cPrimal Virtue\u201d has a similar effect in <b>Mage</b>. <br /> <br /> And other aspects of Primal Utility, such as the ease of creating Wonders, apply to someone accessing the Sphere Variant using Faith rather than Hypereconomics; it's just that Chorister Wonders are going to be religiously significant items rather than technomantic ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:56:26-07:00","id":1300249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300241#post1300241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also imagining that members of any government or non-profit agency or community group could potentially find use for Utility that they invest themselves in and incorporate into their paradigm. An NWO prospect in the IRS who recently awoke but hasn't shown the outward signs may well still develop some form of Utility based on their incorporation of agency procedures and beliefs, and their investment into the same, into their magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Frankly, the brilliance behind Primal Utility isn't really about Hypereconomics at all; it's about saying that there's a special significance in human communities, something that the Traditions would call a mystical significance: there's power in peoples' beliefs, when those beliefs are put into practice. And that needn't be restricted to either Hypereconomics or Faith; as you say, the NWO might see the same thing through their own Focus, with an emphasis on sociology rather than economics. And on the Traditions' side, \u201cPrimal Virtue\u201d needn't be restricted to monotheistic belief systems; though I probably would insist that there be some sort of religious aspect to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T06:15:43-07:00","id":1300261,"title":"","content":"As for Data, I'm personally of the opinion that the restrictions placed on that Sphere Variant are less about the Sphere itself and more about the NWO's Technocratic Focus. In particular, the limitation that the subject must be \u201conline\u201d isn't so much an integral part of Data as it is that the NWO uses the Internet as an Instrument in performing Data Procedures. With their views about the Correspondence Point, I could see the Virtual Adepts Surpassing the need for the Internet and using Data to reach through the unexplored frontiers of the Digital Web (which is far more vast and all-encompassing than the mere Internet is) to connect to people who <i>aren't</i> online. Vulgar as hell, and the VA will likely want to use some sort of communication device anyway, if only for the additional difficulty reduction; but it needn't be an Internet terminal: I could see a VA Data Effect that causes an old rotary phone near the subject to ring, even if said phone is unplugged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T07:04:49-07:00","id":1300271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300261#post1300261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Data, I'm personally of the opinion that the restrictions placed on that Sphere Variant are less about the Sphere itself and more about the NWO's Technocratic Focus. In particular, the limitation that the subject must be \u201conline\u201d isn't so much an integral part of Data as it is that the NWO uses the Internet as an Instrument in performing Data Procedures. With their views about the Correspondence Point, I could see the Virtual Adepts Surpassing the need for the Internet and using Data to reach through the unexplored frontiers of the Digital Web (which is far more vast and all-encompassing than the mere Internet is) to connect to people who <i>aren't</i> online. Vulgar as hell, and the VA will likely want to use some sort of communication device anyway, if only for the additional difficulty reduction; but it needn't be an Internet terminal: I could see a VA Data Effect that causes an old rotary phone near the subject to ring, even if said phone is unplugged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that attempting to access someone with Data when they have no connection to the digital web in a traditional sense (they aren't being observed by CCTV, they don't own any tech etc) is working without Focus unless you have reached a high enough Arete to put the relevant tool aside. So you could access someone with no connection, it would just be +3 difficulty for essentially working without a focus, and 6+ successes to find someone with no connection. Which is far from impossible, but very nasty. And like you say, vulgar as hell.<br /> <br /> What do you think of the other changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T07:15:54-07:00","id":1300272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300249#post1300249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Frankly, the brilliance behind Primal Utility isn't really about Hypereconomics at all; it's about saying that there's a special significance in human communities, something that the Traditions would call a mystical significance: there's power in peoples' beliefs, when those beliefs are put into practice. And that needn't be restricted to either Hypereconomics or Faith; as you say, the NWO might see the same thing through their own Focus, with an emphasis on sociology rather than economics. And on the Traditions' side, \u201cPrimal Virtue\u201d needn't be restricted to monotheistic belief systems; though I probably would insist that there be some sort of religious aspect to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only disagreement is the idea of there needing to be &quot;faith&quot; at least in the religious sense. There needs to be community and investment, IMO. But a secular group could work just as well if it fits the paradigm - a team, a gaming group (especially a networked one with rules imposed from a non-local source - Pathfinder Society or the Mind's Eye Society, for example), any sort of group could theoretically work as long as the group self-identifies as such, sets guidelines as a group and agrees to avmbide by them, takes time to work together towards a common set of goals, and shares a genuine and conscious decision to act as a community with said rules and mores. Assuming, of course, you fit said group into your paradigm.<br /> <br /> But, ymmv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T08:21:58-07:00","id":1300288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300271#post1300271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that attempting to access someone with Data when they have no connection to the digital web in a traditional sense (they aren't being observed by CCTV, they don't own any tech etc) is working without Focus unless you have reached a high enough Arete to put the relevant tool aside. So you could access someone with no connection, it would just be +3 difficulty for essentially working without a focus, and 6+ successes to find someone with no connection. Which is far from impossible, but very nasty. And like you say, vulgar as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly; and all of this follows from \u201cThe Internet is an Instrument\u201d. Again, it's not Data itself that imposes this requirement; it's the use of the Internet as an Instrument in the working of a Data Procedure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300271#post1300271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the other changes?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll get back to you on that. I'm tackling them a bit at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T08:50:16-07:00","id":1300298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300272#post1300272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only disagreement is the idea of there needing to be &quot;faith&quot; at least in the religious sense. There needs to be community and investment, IMO. But a secular group could work just as well if it fits the paradigm - a team, a gaming group (especially a networked one with rules imposed from a non-local source - Pathfinder Society or the Mind's Eye Society, for example), any sort of group could theoretically work as long as the group self-identifies as such, sets guidelines as a group and agrees to avmbide by them, takes time to work together towards a common set of goals, and shares a genuine and conscious decision to act as a community with said rules and mores. Assuming, of course, you fit said group into your paradigm.<br /> <br /> But, ymmv.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying. I used the term \u201creligious\u201d, but I didn't really mean it in the colloquial sense: to me, a Primal Venture (or its equivalent under other paradigms) needs more than just community and investment: if it's just a job or just a social gathering, it isn't Primal. To get to the level where it serves as a source of Quintessence, the community needs to have a sense of meaning, a higher purpose, a vision, that the members of the community truly believe in \u2014 something that they pursue with, dare I say, a religious ferver. <br /> <br /> That's why Hypereconomics requires industry and innovation in order for a venture to be Primal: it's not enough to run a business or to work for a paycheck; you have to be excited about what you're doing, what the venture is seeking to accomplish, and constantly looking for ways to advance the company's goals. It's that higher purpose that I was referring to when I mentioned that there needs to be a religious quality to it in order for it to be Primal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-26-2019, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:42:20-07:00","id":1300326,"title":"","content":"On the Arcane Experience thing: part and parcel with Arcane Experience is the matter of how you go about earning it; and I think this might be a good way to emphasize the Avatar a bit more. That is, consider tying the means by which Arcane Experience is earned at least partially to your Avatar Essence. This is an off-the-top-of-my-head idea right now; but the dynamic between Essence and Resonance really ought to be something to the effect of: you develop Resonance based on your actions, but your actions are influenced by your Essence. Granting Arcane Experience based on Essence-appropriate actions would put some crunch into the latter part while still leaving the character's agency entirely in the player's hands. On the other hand, making Arcane Experience rewards be entirely dependent on your Essence might limit the mage's arcane development a bit too much; so maybe activities relating to all four Essences can earn Arcane Experience, but activities relating to your Avatar's Essence earn more than the others do. <br /> <br /> The trick, then, is to come up with activities for each Essence that involve interacting with the supernatural world (otherwise it wouldn't be Arcane Experience) but do so in a way that plays into that Essence. <br /> <br /> If you're familiar with <b>Promethean: the Created</b>, you might also consider moving that game's Milestones system to represent lessons your Avatar wants you to learn. Or not; the Milestones system can be rather involved. The idea, though, is a sound one: use Arcane Experience as a way to bring the Avatar's agenda a bit more front-and-center in the game, allowing your magickal potential to develop as your Avatar guides you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:54:14-07:00","id":1300329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300326#post1300326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Arcane Experience thing: part and parcel with Arcane Experience is the matter of how you go about earning it; and I think this might be a good way to emphasize the Avatar a bit more. That is, consider tying the means by which Arcane Experience is earned at least partially to your Avatar Essence. This is an off-the-top-of-my-head idea right now; but the dynamic between Essence and Resonance really ought to be something to the effect of: you develop Resonance based on your actions, but your actions are influenced by your Essence. Granting Arcane Experience based on Essence-appropriate actions would put some crunch into the latter part while still leaving the character's agency entirely in the player's hands. On the other hand, making Arcane Experience rewards be entirely dependent on your Essence might limit the mage's arcane development a bit too much; so maybe activities relating to all four Essences can earn Arcane Experience, but activities relating to your Avatar's Essence earn more than the others do.<br /> <br /> The trick, then, is to come up with activities for each Essence that involve interacting with the supernatural world (otherwise it wouldn't be Arcane Experience) but do so in a way that plays into that Essence.<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with <b>Promethean: the Created</b>, you might also consider moving that game's Milestones system to represent lessons your Avatar wants you to learn. Or not; the Milestones system can be rather involved. The idea, though, is a sound one: use Arcane Experience as a way to bring the Avatar's agenda a bit more front-and-center in the game, allowing your magickal potential to develop as your Avatar guides you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh a significant houserule I neglected to mention is that I simply award the same EXP to each player. When playing MTA/VTM/etc. I just prefer to give the same EXP to everyone, it's simpler and avoids me playing the role of being the arbitration on who has earned what.<br /> <br /> With that said, having the Avatar play a bigger role in earning/spending Arcane EXP is a very good idea. Avatars haven't played that big a role so far, but in the long run a Manifest Avatar is going to be a major villain (Mage with a saviour complex is driven towards ascension by his Avatar, who pretends to be a Big Bad to help give him obstacles to overcome; this becomes a problem when the Avatar's actions start leading to people's deaths). But I'll do more to integrate Avatars with the other PCs regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T17:03:37-07:00","id":1300420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300329#post1300329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh a significant houserule I neglected to mention is that I simply award the same EXP to each player. When playing MTA/VTM/etc. I just prefer to give the same EXP to everyone, it's simpler and avoids me playing the role of being the arbitration on who has earned what.<br /> <br /> With that said, having the Avatar play a bigger role in earning/spending Arcane EXP is a very good idea. Avatars haven't played that big a role so far, but in the long run a Manifest Avatar is going to be a major villain (Mage with a saviour complex is driven towards ascension by his Avatar, who pretends to be a Big Bad to help give him obstacles to overcome; this becomes a problem when the Avatar's actions start leading to people's deaths). But I'll do more to integrate Avatars with the other PCs regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible alternative in that case that you hint at - the Avatar and seeking a regulate how you can spend or how fast. Set up a few easy things to spend it on - rotes, low levels of spheres, etc. - and then use the Avatar or Milestone systems as gates for bigger purchases. Maybe look at the Story system from 7th Sea 2nd Ed., if you can get access to it - it used story steps in lieu of experience points (so a two point item required a two step quest, four needed four steps, and so on) but it could be adapted that if you want to spend the experience points you have to meet a certain number of steps (maybe equal to the dots of the item being requested).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:04:38-07:00","id":1300616,"title":"","content":"Okay so I literally just discovered that &quot;Arcane Experience&quot; is a MTAw thing. I just randomly made up the idea and gave it that name because it sounded cool, reflected what the EXP did and rhymed with mundane. Anyways, weird example of 'convergent game design' so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:01:35-07:00","id":1300629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1300211#post1300211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take the Primal Utility thing one step further: I allow other Practices than Hypereconomics to access it. In particular, my Choristers have access to a variation of it where instead of providing access to Primal Ventures that are exceptional examples of industry and innovation, it provides access to Primal Fellowships that are exceptional examples of compassion, prudence, and faith. The game systems are the same, except that investing time and effort to support the Fellowship is preferred over just throwing money their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:22:10-07:00","id":1300632,"title":"","content":"House Rules:<br /> Seekings - No challenge aspect, always succeed. Three options:<br /> Leg work - player helps me do something as an ST like map an area or come up with a cabal of NPCs<br /> Written - player just writes out their seeking<br /> Group - Sometimes, we'll have part of a play session be a seeking where playing characters take on an aspect of the character's past<br /> <br /> Botches - Botches are always complications. They make things worse but never result directly in just damage or failure.<br /> <br /> Buying spheres is done by halfs - first half is rote access, second half is full access. So someone can pay 14 points towards their affinity sphere of Matter to get a fourth dot (28 XP). The character can use matter 4 rotes from tomes and from mentors and teachers at this level. Upon paying the remaining 14 points, the character gets full access.<br /> <br /> XP Costs - I knock a few points off of arete or generally make grimoires available.<br /> <br /> I'm generally loose on having characters who work together a lot work together to make effects.<br /> <br /> Avatars - to me, Avatars are a part of the Mage but still have their own agendas and powers of observation. Characters with high avatars may have to make a willpower roll to do something against their avatar's nature. On the plus side, the avatar can do very minor magickal effects a little below one dot effects. An avatar can indicate that something may be magical but it's on the character to do investigation from there. They also serve a kind of magickal spidersense and allow the character to do counter magick in many cases.<br /> <br /> High Umbra - The high umbra geography is something like:<br /> The City - Contains all fallen epiphanies regarding human activity like the tavern of the four winds, and the fortress of government. Outside of this, it's more or less the Overworld from Scion. The forks of the river of language have areas between them dominated by a spire each containing the pantheon court of some faith or another court . Spires access all epiphanies related to that world view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","user":"PhillyCuriosity","date":".  Added countermagick note. 03-28-2019, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T05:18:47-07:00","id":1305240,"title":"","content":"- In a standard game, with Adult Mages in a normal setting, Resources 1 is given to all characters as default. If a player wants to have Resources 0 they are essentially taking a &quot;1 point social flaw&quot;, and have to RP the consequences of owning basically nothing (crashing at people's homes, staying with other PCs) and having no income.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-16-2019, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T13:46:03-07:00","id":1305547,"title":"","content":"I do something similar with the Avatar Background: it's possible to be a mage without the Avatar Background; but it really ought to be the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T15:29:26-07:00","id":1305580,"title":"","content":"I am thinking about just across the board dropping ability costs to promote a &quot;I'm a wizard I know/can do alot of shit&quot; and get more play on the flavorful but very limited secondary abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T12:28:52-07:00","id":1305782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1305240#post1305240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- In a standard game, with Adult Mages in a normal setting, Resources 1 is given to all characters as default. If a player wants to have Resources 0 they are essentially taking a &quot;1 point social flaw&quot;, and have to RP the consequences of owning basically nothing (crashing at people's homes, staying with other PCs) and having no income.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the way they did this (and a lot of other things) is an artefact of Vampire being the first WoD gameline. It's not uncommon for a vampire to dwell in a sewer or a literal hole in the wall, but humans tend to have more needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 04-18-2019, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:00:56-07:00","id":1306880,"title":"","content":"My only major house rule is that I (as ST) decide when Arete increases and it does not cost XP from the player. This keeps the story progressing evenly and at the pace I want as well as frees up alot of xp for the players to use on skills and what not instead of just spheres and arete. Obviously I get no complaints from the players on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 04-23-2019, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T15:28:29-07:00","id":1343030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules#post1300092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- EXP gets split into Mundane/Arcane EXP. Mundane buys Abilities, Attributes, Willpower, Mental/Physical/Social Merits, backgrounds that Sleepers can have. Arcane buys Arete, Spheres, Supernatural Merits, and backgrounds like Totem and Sanctum.<br /> <br /> The beauty of this is balanced growth is ensured. If you give 2 M and 1 A each session, for example, people develop the Abilities of their mage's practice over time, investing in the WAY their mage does magick, not just in dots in Spheres. People feel empowered to invest large amounts of EXP into things like Etiquette, Expression, High Ritual, Finance and Politics, because they know that they're not &quot;falling behind&quot; in terms of raw magickal power. They know that everyone's got the exact same amount of EXP to put into spheres/arete, so they don't have to sweat the details or worry about the risks of not min-maxing in a competitive game with opposing PCs, for example. I'm seeing the PCs just... flourish, basically, under this system, with loving care going into little details like how they train their abilities and what they plan to do in the future, and even people spending points on frivolous things that don't feed into their magick directly. Plus Attributes and Willpower are so expensive in terms of EXP that I can't imagine PCs investing much in them otherwise, when they can get so much more bang for their buck with magickal stuff.<br /> <br /> Essentially the reason I love this change is that it makes sure that magick is more than what spheres you have, and what arete you've reached. It helps direct the attention of the PCs towards how their abilities feed into their magick, and ensures that the abilities that form their practice get some love. And on top of all of that it means you can give loads of EXP without being scared of the repercussions, and without having to carefully curate what your PCs purchase. Mundane EXP is safe (short of ludicrous amounts), Arcane EXP is potentially dangerous if you give too much, so you can keep that in mind when balancing what you give.</div> </div> </div> </div>Decided I should do an update on this:<br /> <br /> - a Hermetic Harry-potter-like PC realized that his character's paradigm and approach to Magick wouldn't accommodate Life very well. So he began sketching his owl familiar's wings, and the skeletons that his familiar collected. Through continued effort and investment in Art (using Mundane EXP) he reached a point where he felt much more comfortable integrating Life 1 into his character's practice (using Arcane EXP). This has continued to blossom into the PC being something of a Renaissance figure, sketching living beings and prosections (a professionally performed dissection left for people to examine) da Vinci style.<br /> <br /> - the awkward artist PC decided to get into sword fighting, and has become a bit of a reluctant warrior. They're incredibly soft and gentle but they're a big guy and want to be able to protect their friends.<br /> <br /> - the farm-boy PC found some orphaned baby bears and invested a HUGE amount of mundane EXP into Survival and Animal Kinship (at least 15), learning new skills that he didn't have before, just so he could look after these bears and teach them the things their mother would have. These skills are *useful* obviously but it's a great kind of character growth to see a Mage learn new proficiencies just to be kind to animals.<br /> <br /> - the basement hacker PC has started learning tea ritual etiquette and costume design/repair - yes this is motivated partly by them being a huge weeb, BUT they're skills that the player would never have put on their sheet at character generation, and now she's proficient in them.<br /> <br /> There are lots more small examples, but splitting the EXP has been a HUGE success. Best house rule I've ever implemented. Player characters are growing as people, not just Mages, and it's feeding into their Magick in exciting ways. And it leads to much cooler interactions with NPCs - the hacker PC just wants to learn hacking, say, so they interact only with their own computer and maybe a Virtual Adept mentor. But with Mundane Experience liberating their ability to invest, the hacker PC might now decide they should do something about their CRIPPLING social anxiety, and learn some Expression and Leadership - well that might mean interacting with someone with very different views and techniques. And before long it does, inevitably, influence their magick in some way.<br /> <br /> Another advantage I didn't predict is that Arcane EXP does allow for some interesting control, so long as you control when Seekings are possible. If you aren't open to seekings for a certain number of sessions, the Arcane EXP keeps piling up. And that means a PC will end up investing in a new Sphere they've never used before, like Life or Spirit or Time. And that always comes along with them developing a new sense of their character's place in the world, which feels like... you guessed it, perfect training for getting to a Seeking! Rather than PCs just trundling along until they can go &quot;yep it's been long enough, seeking please&quot; they're actively seeking (heh) new ways to grow the whole time, opening up new abilities and Spheres and learning new ways of approaching problems. Which is exactly the sort of lived experience that makes sense as the trigger for further Ascension.<br /> <br /> Because the PCs are so young, I've also put a soft cap on high-leveled Abilities - most of the PCs have one ability at 4, which does make sense... it's strange for a young character to have a highly qualified professional level of ability in one thing, let alone two or three. So the kid who grew up in the wilderness has Survival 4 (Woodland), the kid who was neglected and explored the city has Athletics 4 (Climbing), the kid who spends all their time hacking and posting has Computer 4 (Hacking). But because of that cap, the PCs are encouraged to invest in the Abilities that they have 0 to 2 dots in. Objectively speaking Computer 5 would be an incredible investment for a Mage whose whole paradigm depends on computers, but I'm not happy with that happening for story/authenticity reasons. So instead all that EXP can go towards random stuff like learning the basics of Ninjitsu or Funerary Rites or Whittling (yes, these are all real examples).<br /> <br /> So, try using this if you're starting a new game. It's good. Trust me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 10-22-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:16:07-07:00","id":1343060,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it really qualifies as a house rule, but I use the nWoD/CoD attributes instead of the classic WoD ones. <br /> <br /> I also start characters at Arete 2 automatically. I only start at 1 if I'm doing Initiate level games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:32:28-07:00","id":1343066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1305782#post1305782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the way they did this (and a lot of other things) is an artefact of Vampire being the first WoD gameline. It's not uncommon for a vampire to dwell in a sewer or a literal hole in the wall, but humans tend to have more needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as Mage goes, one aspect (which was somewhat more of a thing in the early material than later) is that the members of the Traditions are essentially part of an underground resistance movement against the totalitarian secret masters of the Western world, and as such frequently have to live off the grid and under the radar of modern society. People like Jack Frost and Tom O'Bedlam in The Invisibles, John Constantine in the early Hellblazer books, and the title character from Meghan Lindholm's Wizard of the Pigeons. I think it mostly depends on what sort of game you're aiming for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T08:56:08-07:00","id":1343594,"title":"","content":"I started using arcane experience and have had interesting results with the players. One thing that always bothered me at other games was the incessant need to limit the use of magic. It was as if mages were penalized for being mages, and it came to the absurdity of tables that players almost never used magic for anything, just social internacional in fear of paradox.<br /> <br /> At my table the players cannot spend experience with Arete, only arcane experience. This experience mod I took from CoD, so that in my game every time players learn something new about the supernatural they get 1 xp arcana point. Of course with certain limitations, such as it cannot be repetitive, It cant be from something they already know, It may come from effects that they didnt known poss\u00edvel or the usage of multiple sphere as long as they have time to undersntand, notice or study It. On nightfolk, said players can learn a lot by even focusing on a singles kind of creatures, like: if you research all cainite base disicplines you would get 1 arcane XP for each=12. This would make said player experts on a certain supernatural subject, which I love the concept of &quot;research&quot;<br /> <br /> It was interesting to see the players capture a vampire for interrogation and experimentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T00:47:50-07:00","id":1343730,"title":"","content":"That would explain why vampires / weird creatures are always kidnapped and tortured, whoever captured them is really trying to get some exp out of them by doing weird shit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T04:16:29-07:00","id":1343745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1343730#post1343730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would explain why vampires / weird creatures are always kidnapped and tortured, whoever captured them is really trying to get some exp out of them by doing weird shit!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really into &quot;earned&quot; EXP, since for me the perfect EXP system is the one where the PCs are all on the same level *unless* there is some reason for them not to be - like a mixed chronicle with Ghouls, Neonates and Elders.<br /> <br /> With that said, I like the idea of Mages getting EXP cost breaks on abilities like Occult and Lore by perusing a Silent Library (one of the ones run by the Kyasid), or gaining cost breaks in Science and Medicine by doing a vivisection on a Werewolf. It kind of highlights the idea of a &quot;power-hungry&quot; Mage who disregards lots of things for power.<br /> <br /> I'm already doing something where a PC can get the 1st dot in a Sphere for 5 EXP (as a one-off) if they spend a while RPing their attempt to learn it - doing something that integrates this new way of looking at Magick into their Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T12:06:29-07:00","id":1343827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1343745#post1343745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really into &amp;quot;earned&amp;quot; EXP, since for me the perfect EXP system is the one where the PCs are all on the same level *unless* there is some reason for them not to be - like a mixed chronicle with Ghouls, Neonates and Elders.<br /> <br /> With that said, I like the idea of Mages getting EXP cost breaks on abilities like Occult and Lore by perusing a Silent Library (one of the ones run by the Kyasid), or gaining cost breaks in Science and Medicine by doing a vivisection on a Werewolf. It kind of highlights the idea of a &amp;quot;power-hungry&amp;quot; Mage who disregards lots of things for power.<br /> <br /> I'm already doing something where a PC can get the 1st dot in a Sphere for 5 EXP (as a one-off) if they spend a while RPing their attempt to learn it - doing something that integrates this new way of looking at Magick into their Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt like doing it in my games. It doesnt make players try harder to improve their own characters since both lazy and any other dedicated player would get the same amount for their effort. It never works, someone will want their deserved XP for their actions, which they should get said boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:11:26-07:00","id":1343863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1343827#post1343827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didnt like doing it in my games. It doesnt make players try harder to improve their own characters since both lazy and any other dedicated player would get the same amount for their effort. It never works, someone will want their deserved XP for their actions, which they should get said boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run games where all the players have busy lives - sometimes a player will miss a few sessions in a row because of illness, or travels, or work problems. It's not a competition, and it's nice and relaxed. If you're completely unavailable for a month it's nice to come back and find you're still on track - you've been missing, but your character has been up to all sorts of things. So we fill in the gap and create a great story. Finn was off caring for some orphaned bears he found, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And at the end of the day my players want to RP, want to succeed in character, want to find things out. They want these things as their own reward. Mechanical incentives like a cost break are just a useful way for me to recognize the effort they've put in - I can see they just enjoy playing the game and don't really need to be &quot;paid&quot; with EXP. I've had zero complaints on everyone getting the same EXP, since the players mostly work together regardless.<br /> <br /> So my personal house-rule is occasional cost breaks, which I keep track of for transparency and to ensure that I remember who has had what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 10-26-2019, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T00:13:17-07:00","id":1343931,"title":"","content":"I want to use the Scourge/Fortune rules from Sorcerers Crusade in a modern setting. Have it as something new (or rather, something old had returned). Why itis happening is unknown. Possibly it could be a long term result of over a decade of the Avatar Storm (which is subsiding somewhat). Or it could be a sign of the new age. Or maybe (insert random whatever). Apply in unevenly, Technocrats still suffer Paradox, with Technomancers it scattered (player's choice). For mystics, it is just the new way of things. Since, say, 2012. Yeah. Initiates have never known another way, and more experience Mages <i>might</i> remember Paradox from when they themselves were Initiates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T09:41:13-07:00","id":1344006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300092-various-mage-houserules?p=1343931#post1343931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to use the Scourge/Fortune rules from Sorcerers Crusade in a modern setting. Have it as something new (or rather, something old had returned). Why itis happening is unknown. Possibly it could be a long term result of over a decade of the Avatar Storm (which is subsiding somewhat). Or it could be a sign of the new age. Or maybe (insert random whatever). Apply in unevenly, Technocrats still suffer Paradox, with Technomancers it scattered (player's choice). For mystics, it is just the new way of things. Since, say, 2012. Yeah. Initiates have never known another way, and more experience Mages <i>might</i> remember Paradox from when they themselves were Initiates.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does Scourge differ from Paradox exactly? I've never really gotten it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T10:44:31-07:00","id":1344019,"title":"","content":"You accumulate points the same way, so at first no one would realize what was happening. You don't suffer backlash. Instead, you gain a point of Fortune with your first Scourge point, and another for every full five points. Whenever you roll Arete, add a number of dice equal to your Fortune score. Nice little boost. It is best if these Fortune dice are a different color.<br /> If any of the Fortune dice come up as a 1, you suffer a Bane. Discharge the whole scourge pool and deal with the consequences (much the same as Paradox). If any of them is a 10 though, you enjoy a Boon. Discharge all scourge, and something good happens to you. If the Fortune dice come up as a mix of 1s and 10s, go with whichever came up the most (ties go to 1's).<br /> <br /> As mentioned, the way I want to use this idea, Technocrats still use straight up Paradox rules. Sitting there smug thinking they have won, the &quot;magickal environment&quot; shifts in favor of traditionalists and mystics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T13:59:37-07:00","id":1344496,"title":"","content":"Scourge was kick ass as fuck because you had a 50/50 chance of the angel you are asking for assistance &quot;I need your Aide (insert angel here) to heal this person&quot; and he would either show up and personally assist you or show up and punch you so hard in the head you explode.<br /> <br /> The example in one of the books also has the fun example of a cultist trying to summon Hecate, and when the final blow is struck to the cultist the ST is just like &quot;Fuck it, lets use both Scourge pools&quot; and they roll a virtue, so the characters accidentally summon Hecate themselves and Hecate just kinda eats the cultist and fucks off.<br /> <br /> Great times all around.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are also slightly different rules for getting rid of Scourge and Scourge tends to manifest its backlashes or boons differently based on your tools (But I've run paradox like this anyway) but those can easily just be handwaved. Example: An Order of Reason member who believes Science is baneful in the eyes of God might have an angel chastise him if he gets a bane.<br /> <br /> A different Order of Reason member might just have his gun explode in his face.<br /> <br /> ETC.<br /> <br /> It kinda helps answer the question &quot;If people explode all the time while doing magick, how do people justify this from a science perspective&quot; and the answer is: because it changes based on your beliefs. (Also the Order of Reason at 4+ arete knew magick existed and believed in Alchemy + Devil worship + Sacred Geometry + God so that kinda helped)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T18:32:08-07:00","id":1345367,"title":"","content":"I use Arete+Sphere for magick dice rolls, but PCs can only roll Willpower #of times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}